IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa24-prosecution`

-- coa24-tests-prosecution.l4: tests for ss 1126 to 1133 (coa24-prosecution.l4). Expected values decided from the text before
-- the run. Dates are worked out by hand. "Three years after" and "twelve months after" are counted with daydate's
-- `add years` and `add months`, which clamp the day of the month (fork F6 in NOTES.md).

§ `Tests for s 1126`

-- (2): England and Wales. ss 458, 460, 949, 953, CA 1985 ss 448-453A and ss 1112, 1112A: the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions.
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (unauthorised disclosure of information)` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 953 of this Act (failure to comply with rules about takeover bid documents)` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 448, 449, 450, 451 or 453A of the Companies Act 1985 (offences in connection with company investigations)` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions`
-- (2)(b): s 798, s 455 of the 1985 Act and paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B: the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 798 of this Act (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 455 of the Companies Act 1985 (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to this Act (breach of certain restrictions imposed under that Schedule)` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
-- (3): Northern Ireland: the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland in place of the Director of Public Prosecutions.
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (unauthorised disclosure of information)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 953 of this Act (failure to comply with rules about takeover bid documents)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 448, 449, 450, 451 or 453A of the Companies Act 1985 (offences in connection with company investigations)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State or the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 798 of this Act (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 455 of the Companies Act 1985 (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to this Act (breach of certain restrictions imposed under that Schedule)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST `s 1126 the Secretary of State alone`
-- Scotland is not mentioned in (2) or (3); another offence is not in the list.
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` Scotland EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) another offence` `England and Wales` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `s 1126(1) another offence` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Brought by or with the consent named: the "except" is met and the section does not itself say the proceedings may be brought.
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` `England and Wales` `s 1126 the Secretary of State` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` `England and Wales` `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Without the consent of a person named: no such proceedings are to be brought.
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` `England and Wales` `s 1126 no one` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` `England and Wales` `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 798 of this Act (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` `England and Wales` `s 1126 the Secretary of State` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 798 of this Act (attempting to evade restrictions on shares)` `England and Wales` `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (unauthorised disclosure of information)` `Northern Ireland` `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (unauthorised disclosure of information)` `Northern Ireland` `s 1126 the Secretary of State` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 458, 460 or 949 of this Act (unauthorised disclosure of information)` `Northern Ireland` `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to this Act (breach of certain restrictions imposed under that Schedule)` `Northern Ireland` `s 1126 the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) another offence` `England and Wales` `s 1126 no one` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `s 1126(1) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A of this Act (false statement offences)` Scotland `s 1126 no one` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for s 1127`

#ASSERT `s 1127(1) summary proceedings for the offence may be taken at the place` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1127(1) summary proceedings for the offence may be taken at the place` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1127(1) summary proceedings for the offence may be taken at the place` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1127(1) summary proceedings for the offence may be taken at the place` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1127(2) section 1127(1) prejudices the jurisdiction` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1127(2) section 1127(1) prejudices the jurisdiction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for s 1128(1): England and Wales`

-- Offence on 1 March 2023: three years after is 1 March 2026. Evidence known on 15 January 2025: twelve months after is 15 January 2026.
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 16 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Evidence known on 15 January 2026: twelve months after is 15 January 2027, but the three years end on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Laid on the day of the offence.
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 1 3 2023) (JUST (Date 1 3 2023)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The date of knowledge is the prosecutor's: not supplied, and the three years not yet over: not covered; the three years over: no.
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An offence on 29 February 2024: three years after, clamped, is 28 February 2027 (fork F6).
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 28 2 2027) (JUST (Date 1 1 2027)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 1 3 2027) (JUST (Date 1 1 2027)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Evidence known on 29 February 2024: twelve months after, clamped, is 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 28 2 2025) (JUST (Date 29 2 2024)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 3 2025) (JUST (Date 29 2 2024)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for s 1128(2): Scotland`

-- (a): not after three years from the commission (offence 1 March 2023: 1 March 2026).
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b)(i): within twelve months after the Lord Advocate's knowledge (15 January 2025: 15 January 2026).
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 16 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b)(ii): where the Secretary of State reported it, within twelve months after it came to his knowledge (1 December 2025: 1 December 2026). Offence 1 June 2024, so three years end 1 June 2027.
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 16 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) TRUE (JUST (Date 1 12 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 1 12 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) TRUE (JUST (Date 1 12 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 2 12 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) TRUE (JUST (Date 1 12 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not reported by the Secretary of State, beyond (i): no.
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 16 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) FALSE (JUST (Date 1 12 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Lord Advocate's date not supplied: not covered, unless limb (ii) is made out.
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 16 1 2026) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 16 1 2026) NOTHING TRUE (JUST (Date 1 12 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 2 12 2026) NOTHING TRUE (JUST (Date 1 12 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 16 1 2026) NOTHING TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 2 12 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for s 1128(3) and (4)`

#ASSERT `s 1128(3) the complaint was made in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1128(3) the complaint was made in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 16 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1128(3) the complaint was made in time` (Date 1 3 2023) (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
